# Only needed for a split deployment, where this web app is hosted
# separately from the API (e.g. this on Vercel, the API on Railway/Render).
#
# Leave both unset for local dev (`npm run dev`, proxied by Vite) and for a
# same-origin self-hosted deployment (both served behind one reverse proxy)
# — the app defaults to relative `/api` and `/ws` paths, which just work.
#
# Vite only exposes vars prefixed VITE_, and inlines them at build time, so
# these must be set wherever you *build* the app (e.g. Vercel's project
# settings), not just wherever you run it.

# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# VITE_WS_BASE_URL=wss://api.example.com
